    fact: "Parker's drink was Scotch; her biographer Marion Meade records that she could manage almost anything in a pinch except gin, which, plain or mixed, made her ill. The martini quatrain universally credited to her (\"After three I'm under the table, after four I'm under my host\") is regarded as spurious, apparently fused over time from a 1944 Bennett Cerf anecdote and an anonymous verse printed in Playboy in 1954. She died of a heart attack on 7 June 1967, aged 73, and left her modest estate to Dr Martin Luther King Jr, a man she had never met; on his assassination the following year it passed, as her will directed, to the NAACP. Told of the bequest, her executor Lillian Hellman reportedly said only, \"She must have been drunk when she did it.\"",
